    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0242" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1910</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d198-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-04T17:00:00+08:47"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1918, 5
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 30, 3.03 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yesterday Soviet notified me they had dissolved City Council and taken over its
                    business. Result cannot be apparent before 8th, as all offices closed till then
                    for Easter holidays.</p>
                <p>All interested posts informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d198-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d198-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Embassy in Japan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
